WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.086 --> 00:00:06.576
Inside the shop Scrooge could see that Wilkins' face had more wrinkles now.

2
00:00:06.577 --> 00:00:11.919
But Wilkins' smile looked brighter than ever as he spoke to a young boy.

3
00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:15.256
"Tell me, Edward," Wilkins said.

4
00:00:15.257 --> 00:00:22.548
"Have you been outside, looking at all the Christmas decorations in the neighborhood?"

5
00:00:22.549 --> 00:00:26.171
"Yes, Grandfather," the boy said eagerly.

6
00:00:26.172 --> 00:00:30.477
"I love all of them—especially the wreaths and garlands.

7
00:00:30.478 --> 00:00:32.312
It's sunny out, but guess what!

8
00:00:32.313 --> 00:00:37.362
It's so cold that the lake in the park is frozen.

9
00:00:37.363 --> 00:00:43.539
I heard people saying they've never seen such a perfect day for ice skating."

10
00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:47.152
"Hmm." Wilkins chuckled.

11
00:00:47.153 --> 00:00:51.741
"It sounds like someone might like to go skating today.

12
00:00:51.742 --> 00:00:56.870
Maybe I can close the shop early, and we can go before dinner.

13
00:00:56.871 --> 00:00:59.467
How does that sound?"

14
00:00:59.468 --> 00:01:05.482
"Really?" Edward said. "We can go skating?"

15
00:01:05.483 --> 00:01:08.957
"Of course," Wilkins said.

16
00:01:08.958 --> 00:01:17.205
"When I opened this shop, I promised myself that I would never let work become more important than family.

17
00:01:17.206 --> 00:01:22.114
And do you know who taught me this valuable lesson?

18
00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:25.503
"Who, Grandfather?" Edward asked.

19
00:01:25.504 --> 00:01:32.197
"A very wealthy businessman named Ebenezer Scrooge," Wilkins said.

20
00:01:32.198 --> 00:01:38.059
"He actually taught me many important things about work."

21
00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:43.055
Scrooge gasped. "This is wonderful, spirit!

22
00:01:43.056 --> 00:01:48.241
Good old Dick Wilkins sounds as if he is quite fond of me.

23
00:01:48.242 --> 00:01:53.888
He always did look up to me when we worked together."

24
00:01:53.889 --> 00:01:58.001
Wilkins reached for a newspaper that was lying on the table.

25
00:01:58.002 --> 00:02:01.752
He opened it to a page with obituaries.

26
00:02:01.753 --> 00:02:08.947
"See this notice, Edward? Mr. Scrooge died recently.

27
00:02:08.948 --> 00:02:14.657
But he was survived by no family, except for one nephew.

28
00:02:14.658 --> 00:02:22.129
And from what I hear, he had no friends at all." Wilkins shook his head.

29
00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:30.772
"It's a shame. I knew him long ago, and he was a nice enough fellow back then."

30
00:02:30.773 --> 00:02:35.316
"Were the two of you once friends then?" Edward asked curiously.

31
00:02:35.317 --> 00:02:39.114
"Well, I tried my best to be his friend."

32
00:02:39.115 --> 00:02:43.105
Wilkins folded the newspaper, setting it aside.

33
00:02:43.106 --> 00:02:46.358
"We worked together for a year or two.

34
00:02:46.359 --> 00:02:53.272
After that, he started a new business with a clever businessman named Marley.

35
00:02:53.273 --> 00:03:02.156
At the time Ebenezer was courting a lovely young woman named Belle who seemed to make him happy.

36
00:03:02.157 --> 00:03:11.319
But with every passing month, Ebenezer spent more time working and less time doing anything else.

37
00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:18.217
I went to visit him a few times, but he had no time for me or anyone else.

38
00:03:18.218 --> 00:03:23.475
He was too busy thinking about money."

39
00:03:23.476 --> 00:03:25.863
Wilkins shook his head.

40
00:03:25.864 --> 00:03:35.484
"Remember this, Edward: A relationship that's neglected will wither and die."

41
00:03:35.485 --> 00:03:37.737
Wilkins suddenly stood up.

42
00:03:37.738 --> 00:03:42.644
"But never mind all that; it's ancient history now.

43
00:03:42.645 --> 00:03:50.288
I'll finish up a couple of things at the shop, and then we can go skating."

44
00:03:50.289 --> 00:03:57.356
Before Scrooge could say anything, the scene faded, and was quickly replaced by another.

45
00:03:57.357 --> 00:04:01.459
He and the ghost now stood in a warm sitting room.

46
00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:07.704
Flower petals were strewn on the floor, and white fabric was draped over furniture.

47
00:04:07.705 --> 00:04:11.627
Belle was there, her hair now touched with gray.

48
00:04:11.628 --> 00:04:17.106
She was beaming at a beautiful young woman wearing a wedding dress.

49
00:04:17.107 --> 00:04:21.343
Belle adjusted one of the sleeves on the young woman's dress.

50
00:04:21.344 --> 00:04:29.240
"There, that looks perfect. I can hardly believe it—my youngest child is getting married!"

51
00:04:29.241 --> 00:04:36.151
Her daughter hugged her. "I'm excited but also very nervous."

52
00:04:36.152 --> 00:04:39.861
"I understand." Belle smiled.

53
00:04:39.862 --> 00:04:46.985
"I was nervous too. But just remember how happy your father has made me all these years.

54
00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:50.966
I can't imagine my life without him."

55
00:04:50.967 --> 00:04:55.445
"You were older than I am when you married him," the daughter said.

56
00:04:55.446 --> 00:04:59.428
"Other men must have courted you before you met Papa."

57
00:04:59.429 --> 00:05:03.264
Belle shrugged. "I suppose they did."

58
00:05:03.265 --> 00:05:06.586
She tilted her head with a thoughtful expression.

59
00:05:06.587 --> 00:05:10.779
"In fact, I nearly got married once before."

60
00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:14.253
"What?" Her daughter looked shocked.

61
00:05:14.254 --> 00:05:20.077
"Why, I never knew that! Who was the man you almost married?"

62
00:05:20.078 --> 00:05:24.241
"His name was Ebenezer Scrooge," Belle said.

63
00:05:24.242 --> 00:05:30.999
"I loved him, but I realized in the nick of time that he loved something else more."

64
00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:35.883
"Oh!" The daughter peered closely at Belle.

65
00:05:35.884 --> 00:05:39.419
"He fell in love with another woman?"

66
00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:46.139
Belle laughed. "No, he fell in love with money, and only that.

67
00:05:46.140 --> 00:05:51.645
And then, thank goodness, I later met my true love, your papa."

68
00:05:51.646 --> 00:05:55.462
Scrooge felt a sharp jolt at Belle's words.

69
00:05:55.463 --> 00:05:59.158
Then Dick Wilkins' words floated through his mind too:

70
00:05:59.159 --> 00:06:05.383
"A relationship that is neglected will wither and die."

71
00:06:05.384 --> 00:06:08.474
Scrooge clutched his head in pain.

72
00:06:08.475 --> 00:06:13.079
"What have I done to myself?" he thought.

73
00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:15.709
He knew the answer.

74
00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:23.930
He had allowed the most precious things in his life to wither and die.

